<title>CHINA: Korean French Banking in step-up FRCD.</title>
<headline>Korean French Banking in step-up FRCD.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>A step-up floating-rate certificate of deposit issue for Korean French Banking Corp will be completed as a club deal, arranger Societe Generale Asia said.</p>
<p>The ultimate size of the issue, launched as a US$60 million deal, would be finalised after the last replies were received, the arranger said.</p>
<p>The certificates have a three-year maturity with annual put and call option.</p>
<p>They pay a step-up coupon of 60 basis points over the London Interbank Offered Rate (LIBOR) for year one, 70 basis points over LIBOR for year two and thereafter, 80 basis points over LIBOR. There is a put-option waiver fee of eight basis points.</p>
<p>A group is being formed.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6960</p>
